# kw-volt-vector: Does vector w=x+1 add a state column w like volt (XPPAUT 8.2.2)?
# xpp: hang
# pc: ODE0019
# ruling: XPPAUT reads vector as a vectorizer statement. It prints Adding vectorizer w and In vector w , is not valid variable, then dies with a segmentation fault (exit status 139), which run.sh passes as hang. A word that starts with ve and has r in sixth place is read this way (kw-volt-vecxxr), any other ve word is volt (kw-volt-vecxxx).
x'=0
x(0)=3
par a=5
aux v=a
vector w=x+1
@ total=0,dt=1
